Slarty wrote:
> 2 Qs:1)Is there some way to tell whether an altar jives with you
> before taking the risk of praying or sacraficing?

A jiving altar??? No idea what you are talking about. Just guessing...
1. Stand on the altar and use command ':' to see whether its alignment
matches yours; don't pray on non-coaligned altars.
2. Whether you are already admitted to pray or not is generally not
easy (i.e. impossible) to calculate (see Wiki for details). Usually
I wait a couple hundred turns before I pray again.
3. Use potions or wands of enlightenment to see whether you can pray.
4. If you sacrifice on an altar; as long as you get "hopefully feelings"
don't pray. It's save if you get "reconcilliation" or if the "hopefully
feeling" messages stopped while sacrificing.

> 2)Is there any reason to pray at an altar, w/out sacraficing.

I use that mostly only for water prayer; drop potions of water on the
altar and pray to get them changed to holy water. (I only pray if I am
in trouble, e.g. if I am very low on HP's or weak from hunger.)

Hope that answers some of your questions. I'm not that proficient in
divine issues.

